# Book :1060 through a callable formal: apply calls its formal op by the name of the contract's formal,
# op(x: value) -- the contract's formals are the callee's (l2_call_head_method: a callable formal of the
# caller first).  apply(inc 10) is 11.  Entry 7.
fn: inc (int: x) int
    return: x + 1
end: inc

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    return: op(x: value)
end: apply

int: ok 7
if: apply(inc 10) != 11
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
